From 998c3358694605495b88af650252b006751f2842 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Micheal Waltz <micheal@ecliptik.com>
Date: Fri, 13 Nov 2026 12:54:10 -0800
Subject: [PATCH] DOS-PORT: patch 0381 -- remove patch 0380 (the TEMPORARY heap
 lock-policy switches DOSAGS_HEAP_UNLOCK / DOSAGS_HEAP_PREGROW_KB): the
 operator keeps both off after round RQ

WHY: 0380 carried two env switches, both off by default, only so one binary could run round RQ's OFF / UNLOCK / PREGROW
ABBA on MS3 (2026-11-13). RQ's pre-registered terms all read SUPPORTED: both levers remove the post-0377 press-18 step
(~150 ms); PREGROW 6,144 KB also cuts the room-2 entry's wall cost by ~890 ms but stops the clock ~3 s once before play,
and its size is per game; UNLOCK only moves the room-2 commit from lost to counted clock and would need an in-run
pageability witness before it could be a default; neither raises displayed frames on MS3 (kept game time becomes more
skips). The operator decided (2026-11-13): keep both switches OFF, revisit only if room-load time becomes a goal. 0380's
message stated the removal: an exact revert if neither became the default.

WHAT: the exact reverse of 0380 (git revert): dos_heap_policy(), dos_heap_policy_report() and the heappolicy /
heappolicy_exit lines leave game_start.cpp and quit.cpp; both names leave the env allowlist. The tree equals 0379's, so the
rebuilt release and instrumented exes are byte-identical to 0379's builds (stamps d5c8fe52808a / e5623c99f752). Re-applying
0380 from git history restores the lever if room-load time ever becomes a goal (records LOCK0380-2026-11-13, ROUNDRQ-2026-11-13).

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
---
 Engine/main/game_start.cpp | 85 --------------------------------------
 Engine/main/quit.cpp       |  4 --
 2 files changed, 89 deletions(-)

diff --git a/Engine/main/game_start.cpp b/Engine/main/game_start.cpp
index 66372dcb3..dc3eb734e 100644
--- a/Engine/main/game_start.cpp
+++ b/Engine/main/game_start.cpp
@@ -41,12 +41,6 @@
